##Lessons Learnt
- That highly descriptive prompts describing a product don't necessarily produce more accurate outputs. That when using image-to-image generation, the prompt should describe the scene and defer to the image for product accuracy.
- By splitting each responsiblity between different agents produced deeper and more accurate outputs than a single combined prompt would have.
- Testing with real data caught product accuracy issues and other errors that never would have been caught reading code alone.

---
##Unexpected Challeneges
- The photoshot counts were being ignored, I'd enter "1 catalogue prompt" and then get 5 back. Agent 1 wasn't told how many shot types to produce, so claude went by its own judgement. This was fixed by giving explicit count instruction.
- I had to use Windows Notepad for the .env file and other files. Notepad kept breaking Python indentation, multiple rounds of debugging by hand editing Python files also kept breaking the code that were hard to diagnose from error messages alone.

